course: dictionary
lesson: 2369
title: Cultural
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Cultural comes from culture, which means the customs, beliefs, food, clothes and way of life of a group of people. Something cultural belongs to that way of life. «Food is cultural: frog legs in France, snails, horse meat in some countries and guinea pig in Peru.» What people eat is shaped by where they live and what they were taught.
explain: Cultural can also mean to do with art, music, theatre and books. «Cultural events» are concerts, plays and exhibitions. Here, cultural means things made for people to enjoy and learn from.
explain: «Cultural differences» are the ways groups of people do things differently. Two children, one in Peru and one in France, may eat different food and celebrate different festivals, and both can be kind and clever. Learning about differences helps you respect them.
explain: Some cultural things are very old. «The Yellow Emperor, Huangdi, is a legendary ruler said to have lived about 4,700 years ago; many Chinese honour him as a cultural ancestor, though historians cannot prove he lived.» Legendary means known from old stories, so the clues tell you that not everything about him can be proved.
fact: Cultural means to do with the customs, beliefs, art, food and way of life of a group of people.
fact: «Cultural events» are concerts, plays and exhibitions.
fact: «Cultural differences» are the ways groups of people do things differently.
fact: «Cultural heritage» means the traditions and things a group of people passes down to the next generation.
fact: The adverb is culturally, as in «culturally different».
exercise: «Food is cultural: frog legs in France, snails, horse meat in some countries and guinea pig in Peru.» What does cultural mean here? | To do with numbers and sums | To do with sports only | *To do with the customs and food of a group of people | To do with the weather
exercise: Which of these is a cultural event? | A spelling test | *A concert or a play | A puddle | A bus timetable
exercise: Mia says «cultural differences» means how people are all the same. What does it really mean? | Rules about crossing the road | *The ways groups of people do things differently | Things that are exactly alike | Good marks in a test
test: «The Yellow Emperor is a legendary ruler; many Chinese honour him as a cultural ancestor.» Which word tells you that a cultural ancestor is someone from a group's past? | Legendary | Ruler | Honour | *Ancestor
test: What is a cultural festival? | A type of weather | *A celebration of a group's traditions, music and food | A test in maths | A kind of shoe
exam: Which sentence uses cultural correctly? | *The town holds a cultural festival with music and food from many countries. | I ate a cultural sandwich for lunch. | The cat is very cultural and sleeps all day. | The bus was cultural and arrived late.
